<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="57966c39-30be-48a6-8aeb-6e20d037a229"><problem><newline/><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64\)</para><para>\(y = -30.84x^2+ 49.61x + 8.99\)</para><para>\(y = -3.72x^2 + 7.34x + 8.67\)</para><para>\(y = -35.78x^2+ 45.21x + 3.74\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(y = -25.41x^2+ 59.28x + 9.64\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--5-->
<para>For questions 5 – 9, use the following information.</para>
<blockquote>The path of a toy rocket after launch is modeled by the following data set. The height of the rocket, in feet, \(y\), corresponds to the number of seconds passed, \(x\).</blockquote>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-bottom="-10" data-left="-2" data-right="7" data-schema-version="1.0" data-tables="[[{&quot;variable&quot;: &quot;x_1&quot;, &quot;values&quot;: [0.4, 1,1.5,2.3,3.5]}, {&quot;variable&quot;: &quot;y_1&quot;, &quot;values&quot;: [20,41,52,60,52]}]]" data-top="70"/>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="b90b03f7-6d4e-43e9-ab11-78fd7d4711c5"><problem><para>
      <para>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the flight of the toy rocket?</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y = -6.1x^2+ 31x + 1.24\)</para><para>\(y = -11.9x^2+ 30.2x + 3.64\)</para><para>\(y = -4.2x^2 + 34x + 6.34\)</para><para>\(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--10 prelude -->
<para>For question 10, Maria has found a curve of best fit using the equation below. </para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-bottom="-150" data-equations="[&quot;y=-0.46x^2+14x+17&quot;]" data-left="-10" data-right="35" data-schema-version="1.0" data-top="300"/>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="50848151-29ad-4f88-a8a1-521249bd70f8"><problem><para>
      <para>Maria is asked to predict the \(y\)-value on her curve when \(x = 10\). To do this, she graphs the function \(x = 10\) and analyzes the intersection point of the curve and the line.</para>
      <para>What is the \(y\)-value Maria is asked to predict?</para>
    </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>10</para><para>93</para><para>105</para><para>111</para></problem><solution><para>111</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 111. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
